floe-gpu-mesa 25.0.7-1+floegpu2
================================

Private GLVND vendor (floe) and matched patched Mesa megadriver. Install
under /usr/lib/floe-gpu. Existing system GLVND dispatches client calls to
libGLX_floe.so.0; the server keeps the system GBM driver.

Client defaults:
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/lib/floe-gpu
  __GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=floe
  LIBGL_DRI3_DISABLE=true
  LIBGL_DRI2_DISABLE=true
  LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE=true
  LIBGL_KOPPER_DRI2=true
  GALLIUM_DRIVER=zink
  LIBGL_DRIVERS_PATH=/usr/lib/floe-gpu/dri

The Xvnc server drops the client-only library/vendor flags and uses the
system Zink/GBM path. Applications may override their own environment.

Qualification requires actual process maps containing the private vendor
AND private megadriver, followed by correct changing window pixels and
the application's actual Zink/Venus/Apple GPU renderer. This package's
build status alone is not graphics or iPad qualification.
